  "title": "Counterexamples to the Baillie-PSW primality test",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Problem (1) Find a counterexample to Baillie-PSW primality test or prove that there is no one.\n\nProblem (2) Find a composite $n\\equiv 3$ or $7\\pmod{10}$ which divides both $2^{n-1} - 1$ (see Fermat pseudoprime) and the Fibonacci number $F_{n+1}$ (see Lucas pseudoprime), or prove that there is no such $n$.",
